<.page_header
  title={gettext("Landing page headline test")}
  crumbs={[
    {gettext("Admin"), ~p"/admin"},
    gettext("Headline test")
  ]}
/>

<div class="card-list">
  <section class="card">
    <h2 class="card__label">{gettext("What is being measured")}</h2>

    <p>
      {gettext(
        "Every logged-out visitor to the start page is shown one of two founder quotes at random and keeps it for their session. Counted per variant: the visitors who saw it, the sign-up forms that created an account, and the PINs that turned such an account into a real member."
      )}
    </p>

    <p
      :if={!@enabled?}
      id="experiment-disabled"
      class="rounded-lg bg-brand-50 px-3 py-2 text-sm text-brand-800 dark:bg-brand-900/40 dark:text-brand-100"
    >
      {gettext(
        "The test is switched off on this installation (LANDING_HEADLINE_EXPERIMENT), so every visitor sees the same headline and nothing new is counted. The figures below are whatever was collected while it ran."
      )}
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="card">
    <h2 class="card__label">{gettext("Result")}</h2>

    <%!-- The two verdicts read first: the numbers below are the evidence, this
          is the reading. Sign-ups are the headline metric Stefan asked for,
          confirmations the harder one (a headline that pulls in people who
          never confirm has won nothing). --%>
    <p
      id="signup-verdict"
      class={[
        "font-semibold",
        verdict_decided?(@report.signup_verdict) && "text-brand-700 dark:text-brand-300"
      ]}
    >
      {gettext("Sign-ups:")} {verdict_text(@report.signup_verdict, @min_signups)}
    </p>

    <p id="confirmation-verdict">
      {gettext("Confirmed members:")} {verdict_text(@report.confirmation_verdict, @min_signups)}
    </p>

    <div class="card__tablewrap mt-4">
      <table class="pure-table">
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th>{gettext("Variant")}</th>
            <th>{gettext("Views")}</th>
            <th>{gettext("Sign-ups")}</th>
            <th>{gettext("Sign-up rate")}</th>
            <th>{gettext("Confirmed")}</th>
            <th>{gettext("Confirmation rate")}</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr :for={total <- @report.totals} data-variant={total.variant}>
            <td>
              <strong>{variant_label(total.variant)}</strong>
              <br />
              <span class="text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400">
                {variant_quote(total.variant)}
              </span>
            </td>
            <td class="font-mono">{delimited_count(total.views)}</td>
            <td class="font-mono">{delimited_count(total.signups)}</td>
            <td class="font-mono">{percent(total.signup_rate)}</td>
            <td class="font-mono">{delimited_count(total.confirmations)}</td>
            <td class="font-mono">{percent(total.confirmation_rate)}</td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>

    <p class="editform__hint mt-3">
      {gettext(
        "Crawlers that ignore cookies count as views, which drags both rates down by roughly the same amount. That is why the verdict above is read from how the sign-ups split between the two variants, not from the rates themselves: a random 50/50 assignment makes an uneven split the signal, and no amount of bot traffic can tilt it."
      )}
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="card">
    <h2 class="card__label">{gettext("By day")}</h2>

    <p :if={@report.days == []} class="card__empty">
      {gettext("Nothing counted yet.")}
    </p>

    <div :if={@report.days != []} class="card__tablewrap">
      <table class="pure-table">
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th>{gettext("Day")}</th>
            <th>{gettext("Variant")}</th>
            <th>{gettext("Views")}</th>
            <th>{gettext("Sign-ups")}</th>
            <th>{gettext("Confirmed")}</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <%= for day <- @report.days, {total, index} <- Enum.with_index(day.variants) do %>
            <tr>
              <td>{if index == 0, do: Date.to_iso8601(day.day)}</td>
              <td>{variant_label(total.variant)}</td>
              <td class="font-mono">{delimited_count(total.views)}</td>
              <td class="font-mono">{delimited_count(total.signups)}</td>
              <td class="font-mono">{delimited_count(total.confirmations)}</td>
            </tr>
          <% end %>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
  </section>
</div>
